  "body": "Closes #1304\nClaim: mac/mac-mbp\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (w1304)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (r1327), APPROVE on f2152877 (round 2; round 1 APPROVE with findings on af36ae93)\n\n### Problem\nSince #1295, `sub`/`sup` read `--context-100` for the floor. A sub/sup inside another one, and a sub inside a quote header (`b.s1`), did not: the header changes the font size without setting the context, and the nested one used the context over 1.2 instead of 1.44. At 100 % that computed 11 px (the floor) instead of the dev-swift size.\n\n### Change\n`reader.css` only:\n- `b.s1` sets `--context-100` (and `--code-100`) to its own size at 100 % (0.85, 0.7225 in code and signature, 0.614125 in a signature code block, of the message text), one rule per existing `b.s1` size rule.\n- `:is(sub, sup) :is(sub, sup)` (and its `table.code` / `table.fixed` form on `--code-100`): `max(1em / 1.2, min(context-100 / 1.44, 11px))`.\n\nRound 1 (review r1327): a third sub/sup level gets its own rule (context / 1.728, and the code form); deeper levels are not covered (they take the third level's size). The closed blocked quote header sets `--context-100` to 0.85 of the message text, so a sub there holds the floor in a signature too.\n\n### Tests\n`ReaderTextFloorWebTests` gains a nested sup, a nested sub in a `[fixed]` block, a sub in a quote header and a sub in a code header, in both existing tests (70 %: within [min(100 %, 11), 100 %]; 100 % and 130 %: dev-swift size times the percentage), roots 17 px and 14 px.\n\n| Element (root 17 px) | dev-swift (100 %) | before fix at 100 % | after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| nested sup | 10.42 | 11 | 10.42 |\n| sub in a quote header | 10.63 | 11 | 10.63 |\n| third level sup | 8.68 | 10.42 | 8.68 |\n| sub in a blocked quote header in a signature (70 %) | at most 10.63 | 9.17 (under the floor) | within [min(10.63, 11), 10.63] |\n\nRed on the previous head (5 failed expectations in round 1; 16 on dev-swift), green after: 68 tests in the 15 reader WebKit suites (the 13 `*WebTests`, ReaderAccessibilityTests, ReaderWebSecurityTests). No other test asserts on these rules.\n\nSwiftLint by hand (test file): line_length 140, file_length, function/type body length, no tuples, no trailing commas, no double blank line. `pre-commit run --all-files` passes.\n\nNo legacy behaviour change: no ledger.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
