   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 1, reviewer r1327 (Opus 5.5), author w1304 (Sonnet 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, r1327, head af36ae93)**\n\n**APPROVE**\n\nComputed against dev-swift before #1295 (parent ÷ 1.2 at each level):\n- nested sup in message text: 10.42 at 100 % (17 px root), 13.54 at 130 %, 10.42 at 70 %, and 8.58 = its 100 % size at 70 % on the 14 px root;\n- sub in a quote header: 10.63;\n- sub in a code header: 9.03;\n- nested sub in a code block: 8.85;\n- sub in a code header in a signature: 7.68.\n\n`--code-100: var(--context-100)` on `b.s1` reads the element's own value, so there is no cycle. Only sub and sup read these variables.\n\n1. **Low**, `reader.css:227-228`. A third level also matches `:is(sub, sup) :is(sub, sup)` and still uses `/1.44`. Scenario: `y<sup>2<sup>n<sup>k</sup></sup></sup>` at 100 % gives 10.42 px instead of 8.68. Fix: a third-level rule (`/1.728`) and a comment on depth, or a follow-up issue.\n2. **Nit**, `reader.css:213` with `:323`. In a blocked quote in a signature, the header keeps `--fs-85-content` while `.signature b.s1` sets `--context-100` to 10.84, so a sub there is 9.17 at 70 %, under the floor. Fix: `--context-100: calc(0.85 * 15 / 17 * 1rem)` on that header.\n\nVerified: `runs/test-red.log` shows the 4 probes failing (16 issues), and `green.out` passes 68 tests in 15 suites. No line over 140.\n\nBoth findings are of the class #1304 fixes. The orchestrator asks for them in one more round before merge.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
