   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 2, reviewer r1327 (Opus 5.5), author w1304 (Sonnet 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, r1327, head f2152877)**\n\n**APPROVE**\n\nComputed against dev-swift before #1295:\n- Third-level sup: 8.68 px at 100 % with the 17 px root and 7.15 px with the 14 px root; 11.28 px at 130 %, as dev-swift; 8.68 px at 70 %, equal to its 100 % size.\n- The code form behaves the same.\n- Specificity: the three-level rule (0,0,3) beats the two-level one (0,0,2) and never matches at depth 2; the code forms (0,1,4) beat (0,1,3).\n- Depth 4 takes the third level's size (8.68 instead of 7.23 at 100 %). This is documented and accepted.\n- Blocked-quote header: its rule (0,3,4) beats `.signature b.s1`, and a sub there is 10.63 px at both 100 % and 70 %.\n\n1. **Nit**, `reader.css:339` and `ReaderTextFloorWebTests.swift:30-31, 84`. The round-1 detail was mistaken: `quote-blocked` is only added to the message text (`TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:126`), never to the signature (`:133`). The declaration and its probe are harmless defence. Keep them or drop them.\n\nVerified: `test-red2.log` on af36ae93 shows 5 issues, and `fix1.out` passes 68 tests in 15 suites. No line over 140.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
